Given a hereditary class $\mathcal{F}$ of finite relational structures, the rank function $\mathsf{rk}:\sigma\mathcal{F}\to\omega_1\cup\{\infty\}$, introduced by Kubi\'{s} and Shelah, measures how far a countable structure is from being universal within its class: $\mathsf{rk}(X)=\infty$ if and only if the Fra\"{\i}ss\'{e} limit embeds into $X$. We say that $\mathcal{F}$ has the Rank Property (RP) if every countable ordinal is realized as the rank of some $X\in\sigma\mathcal{F}$. We develop the…

